# Clinical Sovereignty Lab / Little Nate
# Cursor AI Context Rules

## Project Overview
This is Little Nate, an AI-powered therapy platform with:
- Flutter mobile app (client + coach portal)
- Python FastAPI backend with WebSocket bridge
- React admin console (Sovereign Command)
- Nevedal quantum emotional coherence engine
- Night School AI training system

## Tech Stack
- **Mobile**: Flutter/Dart with Riverpod state management
- **Backend**: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, asyncpg, WebSockets
- **Database**: PostgreSQL 15+
- **Cache**: Redis
- **AI**: Azure OpenAI GPT-4o Realtime
- **Payments**: Stripe (when enabled)
- **Admin**: React with Tailwind

## Architecture Pattern
- MVVM for Flutter (Models, ViewModels, Views)
- Service-based routing for Python (single WebSocket, message dispatch)
- Unidirectional data flow throughout

## Key Algorithms (DO NOT MODIFY without understanding)

### Nevedal Formula
```
C_emo(t) = [β · p_ent · T_tunnel] / [γ_env + E_G^(joint)/ℏ] × exp[-(γ_env + E_G^(joint)/ℏ) × t]
```
Located in: `backend/app/services/nevedal_engine.py`

### Voice Biometrics
Extracts: pitch_mean, pitch_variance, energy, speech_rate, pause_ratio
Located in: `backend/app/services/nevedal_engine.py` → `VoiceBiometricExtractor`

### PII Detection
Pattern-based detection for SSN, phone, email, addresses
Located in: `backend/app/services/night_school_director.py` → `PIIDetector`

## Network Configuration
- Server: 10.0.0.81
- API Port: 8000
- WebSocket Port: 8765
- Admin Port: 3000
- Database Port: 5432

## File Naming Conventions
- Python: snake_case (e.g., `nevedal_engine.py`)
- Dart: snake_case for files, PascalCase for classes
- React: PascalCase for components (e.g., `SovereignCommand.jsx`)

## Important Directories
```
backend/app/services/     # Core business logic
backend/app/routers/      # API endpoints
backend/app/websocket/    # Real-time handlers
mobile/lib/viewmodels/    # Flutter state
mobile/lib/screens/       # Flutter UI
admin/src/components/     # React components
```

## Testing
Run tests with: `pytest backend/tests/ -v`
Flutter tests: `flutter test`

## Environment
All config in `.env` file. Never hardcode credentials.
Key vars: AZURE_API_KEY, DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET

## Design System
- Background: #050505 (void), #0A0A0A (chamber), #111111 (elevated)
- Gold: #C9A962 (primary), #E8D5A3 (bright), #8B7355 (dim)
- Cyan: #4ECDC4 (AI/coaching)
- Purple: #9D4EDD (research)
- Red: #EF4444 (alerts)
- Font Display: Cormorant Garamond
- Font Body: DM Sans

## Terminology
- "Sanctuary" = The platform
- "Threshold" = Trial tier
- "Inner Chamber" = Standard tier ($49/mo)
- "Sovereign Circle" = Top tier ($149/mo)
- "Nate" = The AI companion
- "CEE Window" = Coherent Emotional Engagement moment
- "Night School" = AI training/wisdom system
- "The Dojo" = Adversarial testing environment

## GitHub
Repo: git@github.com:Thera-cloud/Clinical-Sovereignty-Lab.git

## Voice Pipeline Decision (LOCKED)
- Live calls use Grok native voice (Rex) when GROK_NATIVE_VOICE=true (1-hop audio pipeline)
- Fallback: Azure Onyx TTS (automatic mid-call if Grok audio stream fails)
- XTTS on Hetzner is STOPPED and DISABLED (systemctl disable xtts-server)
- Do NOT restart XTTS on Hetzner
- Do NOT set TWILIO_VOICE_PIPELINE=grok_xtts
- XTTS will only be used when a dedicated GPU is available (not shared with firehose)
- The degradation ladder: Grok Rex native → Azure Onyx TTS fallback. XTTS is not in the chain.
- To disable Grok native voice and revert to Azure-only: set GROK_NATIVE_VOICE=false

## When Making Changes
1. Check if algorithm is in "Key Algorithms" section - if so, be very careful
2. Update tests when modifying business logic
3. Keep .env.template in sync with any new env vars
4. Follow existing code patterns in each directory

## PRODUCTION CRITICAL FILES — MINIMAL CHANGES ONLY
These files require explicit approval before modification.
Changes must be additive only: no reformatting, no restructuring, no refactoring existing code.

### Protected Files
- `backend/app/websocket/bridge_server.py` (production WebSocket backbone)
- `backend/app/main.py` (application lifespan + service initialization)
- `backend/app/services/littlenate_inference.py` (core inference pipeline)
- `backend/app/services/nate_memory_crystallizer.py` (crystal promotion engine)
- `docker-compose.prod.yml` (production deployment config)
- `backend/migrations/*.sql` (database schema — additive only, never ALTER/DROP existing)

### Rules for Protected Files
1. Maximum 50 lines changed per commit.
2. No reformatting or whitespace-only changes to existing code.
3. No moving or renaming existing functions.
4. New code must be behind a feature flag.
5. Every change must include a comment: `# QUANTUM-CRYSTAL-ARCH` or `# SOVEREIGN-VOICE`.
6. If Composer/agent proposes more than 50 lines changed, stop and ask for explicit approval.

