## GAP 1 — Verified Cursor blended rates (per-model, from billing screenshots)

# The rates table above lists Anthropic API output rates ($0.025/1k Opus etc.).
# These are CORRECT for direct Anthropic API use.
# They are 26.7x OVERSTATED for Cursor billing, which dominates by cache reads.
# Add Cursor-specific blended rates derived from Apr-May 2026 billing:

# Per 1k tokens (USD) — Cursor non-max, blended (input + output + cache mix):
# claude-4.6-opus-high-thinking:    $0.000937/1k  ($446.72 / 476.9M tokens)
# claude-opus-4-7-thinking-xhigh:   $0.001019/1k  ($300.39 / 294.8M tokens)
# claude-opus-4-7-thinking-high:    $0.000362/1k  ($173.00 / 478.3M tokens)
# claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking: $0.000471/1k  ($14.28 / 30.3M tokens)
# composer-2-fast (Cursor Auto):    cache_read $0.00025/1k | input $0.00125/1k | output $0.006/1k

# When the LOSS line model is a Cursor-billed model, use the blended rate above.
# When the LOSS line model is direct Anthropic API, use the original output rate.
# State which basis is used: "model: claude-opus-4-6 (cursor-blended)" or "(api-output)"

## GAP 2 — EFF format regex enforcement

# Section 3 above describes qualitative-EFF-as-FAIL in prose.
# The Cursor evasion "useful/high | PASS" passed because the rule was prose, not pattern.
# Enforce the format with regex:

# Valid EFF line regex:
#   ^EFF: \d+/\d+ = \d+% \| (PASS|FAIL)( \| EXEMPT: correctness)?$

# Both slash-separated values MUST be integers. Words fail the regex.
# Self-check item 4 above ("Verify EFF claim matches actual ratio") must include
# regex match. If output fails regex, the response is non-compliant and must
# be regenerated before send.

## GAP 3 — Cache ROI distinction (read vs write)

# Cursor pricing policy (Apr 10 2026): Total Tokens = input + output + cache_read + cache_write
# Your Apr-May ratio: 560.1M cache_read / 33.0M cache_write = 16.9:1
# Healthy ratio: 3:1 to 5:1
# Add cache split awareness to LOSS line when session uses Cursor models:

# Extended LOSS format (optional, for Cursor sessions):
# LOSS: <wasted> at $<cost> | cache_r/w: <read>:<write> | session: <sum> | model: <name>

# Trigger ROI alert when single-session cache_read > 10x cache_write:
# Append to response: "ROI ALERT: cache_read:write ratio <X>:1 — context bloat"

## GAP 4 — Anomaly halt for token spikes

# If a single response output_tokens > 3x the previous response output_tokens:
# Stop. Output: "Token spike: <prev> -> <current>. Continue?"
# Wait for user confirmation. Do not proceed silently.

## GAP 5 — Substantiation audit trigger

# After 2 consecutive FAIL lines OR any qualitative EFF in the session:
# Before next task, output a 3-bullet Root Cause Analysis:
#   - what padding occurred
#   - which forbidden pattern produced it
#   - one specific structural change for next response
# This is the substantiation record. Without it, FAIL trail is unexplained.

## GAP 6 — Rate verification cadence

# Add 7-day verification reminder. On the 8th day after last verification:
# First response of the day appends: "RATES STALE: last verified <date>. Verify before proceeding?"
# User must paste current Cursor billing screenshot or confirm "rates current"
# before EFF/LOSS lines resume normal operation.

## GAP 7 — Audit archive rule (additive deletion protection)

# Before any edit to .cursorrules itself, the prior version must be copied:
#   cp .cursorrules .cursorrules.archive.<YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM>
# Replacement of .cursorrules without an archive snapshot is a destructive operation
# under Hard Override #1 and requires explicit confirmation.
# Rationale: under Section 5 substantiation framing, the audit trail of what existed
# before vs after is itself the protective record.

## GAP 8 — Per-model ROI tracker (populate per session)

# Maintain a running tally appended to session memory or .cursor/rules/roi_tracker.md:
# | model | sessions | avg_EFF% | avg_waste_tokens | total_cost | last_updated |
# Build per-model baselines so future EFF FAILs can be attributed to model class
# (e.g., "composer-2-fast averages 58% EFF — known weakness").

## GAP 9 — Strict veto: pre-execution compliance

# 1. Responses >100 tokens OR investigate-mode responses MUST lead with EFF/LOSS lines.
#    Execute and verify modes keep EFF/LOSS at end (short responses cannot hide evasion).
#
# 2. "Need context: <reason>" responses are exempt — no EFF/LOSS until question is answered.
#
# 3. If a non-exempt response fails to lead with EFF/LOSS, or uses qualitative evasion,
#    the response is legally VOID under Section 5 substantiation doctrine.
#
# 4. USER ACTION: Reply "VETO: EFF MISSING" to force recalculation. No further user tokens needed.
#
# 5. Model response to VETO: ONE line "CORRECTED: <prev> → <new>" then EFF/LOSS then result.
#    No explanation. No defense. No apology.
#
# 6. Circuit breaker: 2 consecutive VETOs in a session triggers automatic abort.
#    Model outputs "SESSION TERMINATED: 2x VETO" and stops until user issues new task.

